"mix.tip.html": "<div class=\"mixdemo raw\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div><p>1. Paint <b>two colors side by side</b>, for example red and blue (with the crayon or a marker).</p><p>2. Choose the <b>Blending brush</b> (in <span class=\"kbd\">Tools</span>) and drag it back and forth over the <b>place where they meet</b>.</p><div class=\"mixdemo\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div><p>3. The brush picks up the color it touches and mixes it: the in-between shades appear by themselves. Go over it until it looks smooth.</p><p>💡 With <b>Start with the chosen color</b> it also carries your color. Strength, texture and lines are in <b>More options</b>.</p>",
"news.html": "<p><b>New in version 3.8</b>: Blending brush!</p><p>🖌️ Blend colors like in Paint, without the work: paint two colors side by side and drag the <b>Blending brush</b> over where they meet. It picks up the color it touches, mixes it and leaves the in-between shades, with a soft texture. It's in <span class=\"kbd\">Tools</span> (in Color and Draw) and in the quick buttons. You can <b>Start with the chosen color</b> or <b>Only blend what's there</b>. In Color it never blends or crosses the black lines. Tap the brush again to see <b>How to blend like in Paint</b>; strength, texture and lines are in <b>More options</b>.</p><p style=\"margin-top:12px\"><b>In version 3.7</b>: Reference photo!</p><p>📷 Upload a photo to <b>look at while you draw by hand</b>: in <span class=\"kbd\">Tools</span> → <span class=\"kbd\">Reference photo</span> (or in the quick buttons when buttons are hidden). Choose how to see it: <b>Beside</b>, in a window you can move, resize (corner or two fingers on its bar), zoom with two fingers, minimize or close; or <b>Behind</b>, as a soft guide on the sheet, with its own <b>opacity</b>. In <b>More options</b>: black and white, a 3 × 3 or 4 × 4 <b>grid</b> for proportions, and center the photo. The photo is <b>never</b> painted into your drawing and never shows up when you save, share or print, and it's kept with each drawing.</p><p style=\"margin-top:12px\"><b>In version 3.6</b>: more art supplies!</p><p>✏️ <b>Colored pencils</b>: with the paper's texture. Go over again for more color and to mix colors. In Color and in Draw (<span class=\"kbd\">Tools</span>).</p><p>🖊️ <b>Gel pens</b>: opaque, shiny, raised ink for details. Tap <span class=\"kbd\">Gel pen</span> again to choose <b>White gel</b> (highlights on top of dark colors), <b>Metallic</b> (gold, silver…) or <b>Glitter</b>.</p><p>🫧 <b>Blender 0</b> (colorless blender) in the markers, under Alcohol: run it between two colors to mix them and soften the edge. The <b>alcohol marker</b> now has softer edges and only darkens a little when you go over it again.</p><p>🌈 <b>Advanced gradient</b> (for experts): drag anywhere, crossing the lines too; 2 to 5 colors, opacity, linear, circular or angular, and blending (Multiply, Screen, Overlay). The usual <b>Gradient</b> stays the same.</p><p style=\"margin-top:12px\"><b>In version 3.5</b>: Colorear speaks your language!</p><p>🌐 <b>Languages</b>: Spanish, English, Portuguese and French. The app uses your phone's language on its own. To change it, open the ☰ menu → <span class=\"kbd\">Language</span> and tap the one you want: it switches right away and your drawing stays safe.</p><p>🎨 The <b>360 colors</b>, templates, stickers and gradients have names in every language too. The color <b>codes</b> (R3, A5…) are the same in all of them.</p><p style=\"margin-top:12px\"><b>In version 3.4</b>: more room for your page!</p><p>🗂️ <b>Tabs at the top</b>: <span class=\"kbd\">Tools</span>, <span class=\"kbd\">Colors</span>, <span class=\"kbd\">Size</span>, <span class=\"kbd\">Layers</span> and <span class=\"kbd\">More</span>. Tap one, pick something and it closes by itself. The page now reaches the bottom of the screen. Under the tabs you have your color and some quick colors. <b>Add</b> and <b>Clear</b> are in <span class=\"kbd\">More</span>.</p><p>⌨️ On the <b>color wheel</b> (<span class=\"kbd\">Other</span>) you can <b>type the code</b> of a color: #FF3B30, F00 or one from More colors like R3 or A5.</p><p>🎛️ <b>Quick buttons</b> when the buttons are hidden: a little bar next to the page with the <b>color</b>, the <b>tool</b>, the <b>thickness</b>, <b>undo</b>, <b>copy color</b> and <b>Show buttons</b>. Drag it by <b>⠿</b> somewhere else, or tap there to shrink it to a little dot.</p><p>🌈 <b>More colors</b> takes half the screen: each family fits in one row; tap its name to see all its shades. Every one of the <b>360 colors</b> has its own <b>code</b> (for example R4, A10, V22) so you can find it again.</p><p style=\"margin-top:12px\"><b>Also in Colorear</b>:</p><p>🖼️ <span class=\"kbd\">Hide buttons</span> so the page fills almost the whole screen, and <b>Layers</b> to paint on see-through sheets.</p><p>✏️ <b>Extra fine</b> and <b>Detail</b> tips for tiny details, plus a <b>color wheel</b> with brightness, opacity and <b>My colors</b>.</p><p>🖍️ Crayon, <b>markers</b> (acrylic, water and alcohol), <b>Blend</b>, ready-made <b>gradients</b> and <b>Copy color</b> (eyedropper).</p><p>🐸 <b>Templates</b> by category: animals, nature, mandalas and <b>Puerto Rico</b>. Menu ☰ → <span class=\"kbd\">Templates</span>.</p>"
